<!-- is:inline so Astro leaves the snippet alone. The router keeps this head
     script across navigations; the guard makes sure it never inits twice anyway.
     The project token is public by design.

     One change to PostHog's snippet: it no longer adds array.js right away
     but exposes that as posthog.__load, called once the page is idle (or on
     the first interaction, if that comes sooner). The stub queues every call
     until then, so nothing is lost unless the visitor leaves within seconds.
     That keeps PostHog's ~0.5s of script off a phone's first load. -->
<script is:inline>
  if (!window.__posthog_initialized) {
    window.__posthog_initialized = true
    // PostHog's snippet, kept minified as they ship it (with the __load
    // change above), so it's easy to diff against theirs: neither Prettier
    // nor ESLint touches it.
    // prettier-ignore
    // eslint-disable-next-line
